course: dictionary
lesson: 6551
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A newspaper can mean more than one thing, so check the words around it. «She reads the newspaper with her breakfast.» Here it means the printed sheets full of news, because you read them at breakfast.
explain: «The newspaper hired three new writers.» Here it means the company that makes the paper, because a company hires people. Use the clue to choose the meaning.
explain: «We covered the tables with newspaper before painting.» This means old sheets of paper used to protect things or for crafts. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you chose well.
fact: A newspaper is large folded sheets of printed paper with news, stories, pictures and adverts.
fact: Newspapers are published every day or every week.
fact: A newspaper can also mean the company that makes it.
fact: Old newspaper, which you cannot count, is used for wrapping, painting and crafts.
fact: A newspaper report has a headline and answers the 5 Ws: who, what, where, when and why.
exercise: «She reads the newspaper with her breakfast.» What is a newspaper here? | *Folded sheets of printed paper with news and pictures | A box for keeping letters | A kind of cake | A school that teaches reading
exercise: «We covered the tables with newspaper before painting.» What does newspaper mean here? | *Old sheets of paper used for protecting things and crafts | A map of the town | A daily story told by the teacher | A company that hires writers
exercise: «A newspaper report answers the 5 Ws.» Which of these is one of the 5 Ws? | column | caption | headline | *when
test: «The newspaper company hired three new writers.» What does newspaper mean here? | Sheets of paper for wrapping fish | *A company that makes newspapers | A poster on the wall | A weekly magazine of games
test: Sam reads a story in the newspaper. Why should he check the facts? | Checking is only for maths | *Not everything printed is true, so check it in more than one place | Newspapers never have stories about real people | Printed words are always true, so no check is needed
exam: «Think of your class newspaper with ten stories and room for four.» Why does choosing the stories matter? | The stories must all be the same length | Choosing has no effect on anyone | Only the teacher is allowed to read it | *Whoever chooses decides what everyone thinks matters
